==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|s|u}}

===Etymology===
Cognate with Estonian {{term|lang=et|surm}}.

===Noun===
{{fi-noun|surm|type=koira}}

# Violent [[death]], especially a [[kill]].
#:''he saivat surmansa'' (they got killed; literally: “they got their deaths”)
# [[personification|Personification]] of sudden [[death]].
#:''hän joutui surman suuhun'' (he got into the mouth of death)
# {{law|lang=fi}} [[voluntary manslaughter|Voluntary manslaughter]] (''less aggravated than [[tappo]], as it is committed under mitigating circumstances'')

====Usage notes====
*(''law:'') The order of homicidal crimes &mdash;by how severe they are considered in Finnish law&mdash; is (from the least aggravated to the most aggravated) [[kuolemantuottamus]] ("involuntary manslaughter") -> [[surma]] ("voluntary manslaughter under mitigating circumstances") -> [[tappo]] ("voluntary manslaughter" or "homicide", under no mitigating circumstances) -> [[murha]] ("murder", "homicide", killing of a person by another under aggravating circumstances, premeditated and/or brutal).

